    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a derived response field, so I put it alongside the other derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) rather than in the entity or a request pipeline step:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression and a small `membershipTier(Owner)` default method that returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, else `BRONZE` (with null-guards for both source fields, matching the style of the existing `membershipNumber` mapping).\n\nNo new class was needed \u2014 the mapper already owns owner-DTO derivation, so this reuses that single-responsibility home. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
